                "senderName": "NWS Juneau AK",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 16 at 8:30AM AKDT until October 16 at 1:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
                "description": "Rain showers following a strong system continues through Friday\nmorning, keeping potential for flooding along small creeks. Multiple\nwaves moving up brought  persistent moderate to heavy rain for much\nof the southern half of the panhandle, with the heaviest rain\nexpected through Thursday night.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The following areas, Central Inner Channels, Southern Inner\nChannels and Southeast Gulf Coast. This includes the cities of\nPetersburg, Kake, Port Alexander, Craig, Klawock, Hydaburg, Coffman\nCove, Thorne Bay, And Wrangell.\n\n* WHEN...Until 1 PM AKDT this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, other low-lying areas and flood-prone locations.\nStreet flooding and flooding of creeks and rivers are possible.\nIsolated landslides are possible in areas of steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Rain amounts have reached around 3 to 5 inches, with higher rain\ntotals falling by the morning along favoring southern facing\nmountain sides. While the heavy rain has largely ended this\nmorning, the multiple rounds of heavy rainfall from Thursday and\novernight keep potential for flooding and ponding over roads into\nthe morning hours.",
                "instruction": "Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nYou should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.\n\nThe ongoing rains could swamp boats. Mariners should check their\nvessels immediately.\n\nAll residents on or near mountain slopes should be prepared for\npossible landslides.",
                "response": "Prepare",
